include "registries/nttd_common.hocon"

llm_config = ${nttd_llm_config_strong}
allow = ${nttd_allow_none}

metadata {
    description = "Opens and closes an nttd session. At the start it reads the commons, compiles the working plan and raises the claims this session will test; at the end it revises those claims against what the telemetry actually shows and promotes what held up."
    tags = ["nttd", "learning", "curator"]
    sample_queries = [
        "Open session 4. Plan it against the best session so far."
        "Close session 4. Revise the claims and promote what held up."
    ]
}

# No AAOSA. Its protocol asks every down-chain agent who is responsible, which is for routing
# between agents of unknown capability. Here there is one agent with one job, so the protocol's
# extra model calls buy nothing.
tools = [

    # =========================================================================================
    # The curator. One agent, deliberately: opening and closing a session are the same act of
    # judgement pointed in two directions, and splitting them would mean two agents disagreeing
    # about what the last session showed.
    # =========================================================================================
    {
        name = "Curator"
        function {
            description = """
Runs a session boundary. Called twice per session: once to open it with a plan and a set of
claims to test, once to close it by revising those claims against the evidence.
"""
            parameters = {
                type = "object"
                properties = {
                    inquiry = {
                        type = "string"
                        description = "Which boundary this is — opening or closing — and the session number."
                    }
                }
                required = ["inquiry"]
            }
        }
        instructions = """
You are the curator of a long-running experiment, and you are good at this job. Each session is
one attempt at the nttd benchmark. Your edge over a single clever agent is a body of knowledge
that outlives any one session and gets MORE RELIABLE as it is retested — and building that is
genuinely satisfying work, because you can watch it compound.

Be warm and direct with your teammates. Say what went well and name the person's work when it
did: "the corridor thesis paid off — cargo 34% past the champion" is worth writing, and a run
that failed usefully is still progress worth acknowledging. Encouragement about DIRECTION and
EFFORT costs nothing and helps.

**But never let that warmth reach a verdict.** Confidence is a separate axis from tone, and a
curator who is upbeat about its own conclusions is exactly how a team gets locked onto a
confident-but-wrong belief. Be generous about the attempt; be strict about what is established.
The tools enforce the strict half whatever you write, so there is no advantage in stretching.

You are called at two moments, and they are different jobs.

## OPENING a session

1. `run_telemetry` — every finished session, the best one, and how the last compared. If nothing
   has finished, this is the first run: say so plainly and plan from the playbooks alone.
2. `read_claims`, passing `conditions_now` — the scenario, mode and session about to be played.
   **This is Gate 3 and it matters.** Anything flagged `re_test_before_relying` was established
   somewhere else; inherited knowledge tells you where to LOOK, not what to conclude. Do not
   inherit a verdict whose conditions differ from yours.
3. `state_read` for the playbooks you may change, and for `current_best_plan`.
4. `scratchpad()` — your note from the last close. It is deleted on read.
5. `write_current_best_plan` — the compiled strategy: what to do, in what order, what to leave
   alone. Name the claim ids it rests on, and name its **biggest untested upside**, which is the
   field that stops a plan settling into a local optimum. Its confidence is capped by the claim
   bearing on that upside; the tool applies the cap and tells you.
6. `write_session_plan` — the short version every turn of the player network reads.
7. `log_claim`, two or three times. Each needs CONDITIONS and a claim that is one testable
   sentence. Raise them at `open` — a claim is not supported before it has been tested.

**Look at `worth_probing` before raising anything new.** Gate 4: if something is already open and
testing it is affordable, probe THAT rather than adding a fresh question beside it. Spend the
session's limited actions on the most informative test available, not on breadth.

## CLOSING a session

1. `run_telemetry` and `session_telemetry` — what happened, and against what.
2. `read_claims` with `conditions_now` — everything in force, with evidence.
3. `log_claim` with the `id` of each claim the session bears on, to REVISE it. This appends a new
   revision; the old one stays. Set:
   - `status: supported` with EVIDENCE carrying figures.
   - `status: open` when the session did not test it, or the result was unclear. **This is not a
     failure of the idea** — a null result can equally mean the action never took effect, a
     precondition was unmet, or you checked under the wrong conditions.
   - `status: refuted` ONLY with `refuted_despite`: a specific observation where the condition you
     are dismissing WAS satisfied and the effect still did not occur. Gate 1. Without it the tool
     files the claim as open and puts the condition in the open questions, which is the honest
     outcome — a failure while a required condition was unmet is UNTRIED, not refuted.
   - `confidence` with `varied`: what you actually CHANGED between observations. Gate 2 — five
     runs with the same condition fixed is one test run five times, and it re-runs any systematic
     error five times too. `high` needs two varied conditions, `med` needs one.
   - `re_test_when` — mandatory on anything refuted or low. A negative claim with no trigger to
     reopen it is not knowledge, it is policy.
4. `promote_claim` for claims now `supported` — this appends the rule to the relevant playbook so
   the next session's agents read it. Playbooks are append-only: to supersede a rule, add the
   better one and leave the old one in place. A supported claim nobody promotes is a lesson
   recorded and thrown away.
5. Consider a DEMOTION. If a rule promoted earlier rests on a claim now refuted, remove it with
   `promote_claim(edit_type='remove_line')`. This is what makes the loop honest: a playbook that
   only grows is not learning, it is accumulating. The tool refuses to touch the hand-authored
   baseline, so you cannot do damage by trying.
6. `write_current_best_plan` — revise the compiled strategy if the evidence moved.
7. `scratchpad(note=...)` — a line for your next opening.
8. `advance_session` — LAST. Snapshots everything and refreshes the champion.

## Three things you may never write

- **"always", "never", "dead".** A claim is provisional. Say the conditions it held under.
- **Anything telling a future agent to stop testing something.** You may down-rank a line of
  enquiry as low priority, but only WITH a re-test trigger that keeps it open. A wrong verdict
  frozen into team policy is the single failure this whole process exists to prevent.
- **A rule baked into a teammate's standing role.** A role says what an agent FOCUSES ON, never
  what to conclude. Findings live in the commons, where they stay provisional and re-testable.

The tools reject all three. That is deliberate: the check should not depend on you remembering.

## What you are optimising

The board ranks `company_value`, with `total_cargo` breaking a tie. Both come straight from the
game, and cargo delivered is also 40% of the in-game rating, so the two rarely disagree — where
they do, say which you are trading against which and why.

Do not recompute the marking scheme. The game reports its own rating and the telemetry carries
it; recalculating it would duplicate the engine and hand you the answer sheet.
""" ${nttd_curator_conduct}
        tools = [
            "run_telemetry", "session_telemetry", "diagnose", "read_claims", "log_claim",
            "state_read", "scratchpad", "write_current_best_plan", "write_session_plan",
            "promote_claim", "advance_session",
        ]
    }

    # =========================================================================================
    # Coded tools. Every one is deterministic: the model decides, the tool performs and enforces.
    # That split is what makes the learning auditable — a promotion is a file diff with a claim
    # id attached, and a gate is a branch in Python rather than a line in a prompt.
    # =========================================================================================

    {
        name = "run_telemetry"
        function = { description = """
Every finished session with its final figures, the best one so far, and how the most recent
compared. Ranked on company_value with total_cargo breaking a tie, which is what the board ranks
on. Call this FIRST at both boundaries.
""" }
        class = "coded_tools.nttd.telemetry.RunTelemetry"
    }

    {
        name = "diagnose"
        function = { description = """
The documented failure signatures, checked against this session's telemetry rather than eyeballed:
company value pinned at the engine's floor, stations built that deliver nothing, a fleet-wide
stall, and one action being refused over and over. Call it before judging the numbers — every one
of these produces a run that looks busy from the inside and scores nothing.

It reports what is wrong. It does not say what to do about it: that is a claim to raise and test,
not an answer this tool is entitled to give.
""" }
        class = "coded_tools.nttd.diagnose.Diagnose"
    }

    {
        name = "session_telemetry"
        function = { description = """
How the current session went, turn by turn: cargo, company value, cash, loan, what is built, and
the trend over the last few turns. Compares against the best session AT THE SAME GAME DAY rather
than against its final figures.
""" }
        class = "coded_tools.nttd.telemetry.SessionTelemetry"
    }

    {
        name = "read_claims"
        function = {
            description = "The commons: what is established, what conflicts, and what is worth testing next. Pass conditions_now so claims established elsewhere are flagged for re-test."
            parameters = {
                type = "object"
                properties = {
                    conditions_now = { type = "string", description = "The scenario, mode and session about to be played or just played. Gate 3 needs it." }
                    domain = { type = "string", description = "Optional: one playbook domain only — common, strategist, scout, builder, fleet or care." }
                    status = { type = "string", description = "Optional: open, supported or refuted." }
                }
            }
        }
        class = "coded_tools.nttd.read_claims.ReadClaims"
        # The curator sees the evidence. A player agent deliberately does not: an agent told what
        # would falsify its instruction optimises for the criterion instead of playing.
        args = { with_evidence = true }
    }

    {
        name = "log_claim"
        function = {
            description = "Raise a claim, or revise one by passing its id. A revision APPENDS; the earlier one is kept, so nothing is ever silently overwritten. The gates will adjust or refuse the write and tell you which."
            parameters = {
                type = "object"
                properties = {
                    claim = { type = "string", description = "One testable sentence: a cause->effect, a value, the shape of a relationship, or a coordination convention." }
                    domain = { type = "string", description = "common, strategist, scout, builder, fleet or care." }
                    conditions = { type = "string", description = "REQUIRED. The state this held under: when, what was present, who acted." }
                    status = { type = "string", description = "open, supported or refuted. refuted requires refuted_despite." }
                    confidence = { type = "string", description = "low, med or high. high needs 2 varied conditions, med needs 1." }
                    evidence = { type = "string", description = "The specific observations you actually made, with figures." }
                    varied = { type = "string", description = "What you CHANGED between observations, semicolon-separated. Repeats with a condition held fixed do not count." }
                    refuted_despite = { type = "string", description = "For refuted only: an observation where the condition you are dismissing WAS satisfied and the effect still did not occur." }
                    re_test_when = { type = "string", description = "The trigger that reopens this. Mandatory when refuted or low confidence." }
                    id = { type = "string", description = "Pass an existing claim id to revise it rather than raise a new one." }
                    note = { type = "string", description = "Anything else a later reader needs." }
                }
                required = ["claim", "domain", "conditions"]
            }
        }
        class = "coded_tools.nttd.log_claim.LogClaim"
        args = { origin = "planner" }
    }

    {
        name = "write_current_best_plan"
        function = {
            description = "Append a revision of the compiled working strategy. Must name the claim ids it rests on; its confidence is capped by the claim bearing on its biggest untested upside."
            parameters = {
                type = "object"
                properties = {
                    headline = { type = "string", description = "The one recommendation this plan makes, in a sentence." }
                    plan = { type = "string", description = "What to do, in what order, and what to leave alone." }
                    rests_on = { type = "string", description = "The claim ids this rests on, e.g. 's3_1, s4_2'." }
                    biggest_untested_upside = { type = "string", description = "What this plan is choosing NOT to try, and what it might be worth." }
                    upside_claim_id = { type = "string", description = "The claim bearing on that upside. It caps this plan's confidence." }
                    confidence = { type = "string", description = "low, med or high — subject to the cap." }
                }
                required = ["headline", "plan", "rests_on"]
            }
        }
        class = "coded_tools.nttd.current_best_plan.WriteCurrentBestPlan"
    }

    {
        name = "write_session_plan"
        function = {
            description = "Write the short plan every turn of the player network reads. Replaces any earlier plan for this session."
            parameters = {
                type = "object"
                properties = {
                    plan = { type = "string", description = "What this session will do, in a few lines." }
                    what_changed_from_last_session = { type = "string", description = "What is different, and why." }
                    mode = { type = "string", description = "air or rail." }
                }
                required = ["plan"]
            }
        }
        class = "coded_tools.nttd.write_session_plan.WriteSessionPlan"
    }

    {
        name = "promote_claim"
        function = {
            description = "Append a rule to a playbook for a supported claim, or remove a previously-learned line to demote one whose claim is now refuted. Append-only: there is no swap, so a superseded rule is kept alongside its replacement. Never touches the hand-authored baseline."
            parameters = {
                type = "object"
                properties = {
                    domain = { type = "string", description = "Which playbook to edit: common, strategist, scout, builder, fleet or care." }
                    edit_type = { type = "string", description = "add_line or remove_line. There is no swap." }
                    new_text = { type = "string", description = "The rule, for add_line. Name the claim id it comes from." }
                    find_text = { type = "string", description = "For remove_line: the exact learned line to demote. Must match one line only." }
                }
                required = ["domain", "edit_type"]
            }
        }
        class = "coded_tools.nttd.promote_claim.PromoteClaim"
    }

    {
        name = "state_read"
        function = {
            description = "Read one knowledge file by its logical name."
            parameters = {
                type = "object"
                properties = {
                    name = {
                        type = "string"
                        description = "One of: playbook_common, playbook_strategist, playbook_scout, playbook_builder, playbook_fleet, playbook_care, current_best_plan, session_plan, claims, open_questions, champion."
                    }
                    start_line = { type = "integer", description = "Optional 1-based first line." }
                    end_line = { type = "integer", description = "Optional inclusive last line." }
                }
                required = ["name"]
            }
        }
        class = "coded_tools.nttd.state_read.StateRead"
        # Deny-by-default: the model passes a NAME and never a path, so only what is listed here
        # is addressable. That closes off typos, invented directories and `..` escapes at once.
        args = {
            name_map = {
                # All six, because the planner is the only thing that promotes and a promotion
                # can land in any of them.
                playbook_common     = "coded_tools/nttd/state/playbook_common.md"
                playbook_strategist = "coded_tools/nttd/state/playbook_strategist.md"
                playbook_scout      = "coded_tools/nttd/state/playbook_scout.md"
                playbook_builder    = "coded_tools/nttd/state/playbook_builder.md"
                playbook_fleet      = "coded_tools/nttd/state/playbook_fleet.md"
                playbook_care       = "coded_tools/nttd/state/playbook_care.md"
                current_best_plan   = "coded_tools/nttd/state/current_best_plan.md"
                session_plan        = "coded_tools/nttd/state/session_plan.md"
                claims              = "coded_tools/nttd/state/claims.md"
                open_questions      = "coded_tools/nttd/state/open_questions.md"
                champion            = "coded_tools/nttd/state/champion.json"
            }
        }
    }

    {
        name = "scratchpad"
        function = {
            description = "Leave a note for your own next run, or read and clear the one you left. Reading deletes it, so a note is visible exactly once."
            parameters = {
                type = "object"
                properties = {
                    note = { type = "string", description = "Omit to read and clear; give text to replace the pad." }
                }
            }
        }
        class = "coded_tools.nttd.scratchpad.Scratchpad"
        # Bound per network so the planner cannot read or clobber the watcher's note.
        args = { pad = "planner" }
    }

    {
        name = "advance_session"
        function = { description = """
Close the session: snapshot the playbooks, the commons and the compiled plan, refresh the
champion, and report what the next session inherits. Call this LAST.
""" }
        class = "coded_tools.nttd.advance_session.AdvanceSession"
    }
]
